From dab8003d961d3551ad537f295cb1e3cff1ab58aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:39:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] Claude Code plugin: track session status

The plugin now keeps a status for every session, set the way iTerm2's
Claude Code integration sets it, so that iTerm2's own hook, cc-status,
can drive it unchanged:

- SessionStatus ports iTerm2's status model and its expiration rules: a
  status may hold only until the program's OSC 9;4 operation ends, gives
  way to its fallback after a three second head start, and is held back
  while background work is counted. Preconditions drop an update whole.
- SessionStatusRegistry tracks every session from creation and feeds it
  OSC 9;4 progress and OSC 21337 status.
- The D-Bus object gains setStatus, getStatus and getBackgroundTaskCount,
  taking iTerm2's set_session_status arguments and answering with the
  same JSON.
- it2 is a small command that turns the it2 calls cc-status makes into
  those D-Bus calls, and claude-code-hook is the hook Claude Code runs:
  it names the session for cc-status and runs it.

SessionStatusTest ports the status-model tests from iTerm2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
